The relay shell's reader awaits each stream's consumer inline (it reads on only once every delivered byte was taken)
instead of queueing: one stream whose consumer stops reading stops the whole channel. Both small-pipe tests
(runtime/crates/drgnx-px/tests/small_pipes.rs) time out under it.

